1
00:00:02,450 --> 00:00:04,975
{\an8}The dock is the toolbar of your dash.

2
00:00:05,550 --> 00:00:07,850
{\an8}Open Dock to customize it.

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:12,950
{\an8}You can add more docks, for extra buttons or quick settings.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:17,000
{\an8}Place each one on the right, at the bottom or at the top.

5
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:21,025
{\an8}Sides already in use are not offered.

6
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:24,200
{\an8}Select a dock to see its buttons.

7
00:00:26,250 --> 00:00:29,225
{\an8}The left dock has more buttons than you can see.

8
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:34,700
{\an8}Hold Shift and scroll to move left and right.

9
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:42,125
{\an8}Use Search buttons and apps to find a function.

10
00:00:42,750 --> 00:00:46,300
{\an8}Select a button and remove it from the list on the left.

11
00:00:47,050 --> 00:00:49,100
{\an8}Let's fill the bottom dock.

12
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:54,900
{\an8}Click a function to add it.

13
00:00:57,050 --> 00:00:59,050
{\an8}Buttons shrink to make room.

14
00:01:04,750 --> 00:01:07,600
{\an8}When the dock is full, you can't add any more.

15
00:01:08,050 --> 00:01:11,650
{\an8}Shape, size and position are all set here, in Dock.
